{{Quote|Alert the Resistance&hellip; their missing droid is here!|translated=1|GA-97 reports sighting BB-8|<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>}}
'''GA-97''' was an unassuming [[GA-series servant droid|GA-series]] [[Service droid|servant droid]] who served at the [[Takodana Castle|castle]] of the [[pirate]] [[Maz Kanata]] on the [[planet]] [[Takodana]], but was secretly aligned with the [[Resistance]]. In the [[Standard year|year]] [[34 ABY]], it was present when the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] entered with the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], the former [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] [[Finn]] and the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]]. Recognizing BB-8 as a missing Resistance [[droid]], GA-97 contacted them via their [[Resistance spy droid network|intelligence network]] to inform them of the astromech's location. Based on the droid's report, Resistance forces were mobilized to travel to Takodana. Before they arrived the castle was [[Battle of Takodana|destroyed]] in an attack by the [[First Order]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Your droid is on Takodana.''"<br />"''Isn't that&hellip; Maz Kanata's place?''"<br />"''Yup. Two people just walked right in with him. We got a call from one of Threepio's operatives stationed there&mdash;GA-97.|Leia Organa and [[Poe Dameron]] speaking of BB-8|<ref name="Poe Dameron 26">[[Poe Dameron 26|''Poe Dameron'' 26]]</ref>}}
[[File:GA-97_reports.png|thumb|left|200px|GA-97 reported BB-8's presence on Takodana to the Resistance.]]
GA-97<ref name="TFAVD" /> was a [[GA-series servant droid|GA-series]]<ref name="TFA Junior Novel" /> [[Service droid|servant droid]] that was aligned with the [[Resistance]] during their [[Cold War|conflict]] with the [[First Order]] and plugged into [[Resistance spy droid network|their intelligence network]].<ref name="TFAVD" /> The [[droid]] was spending time in the [[Takodana Castle|castle]] of the [[pirate]] [[Maz Kanata]] on the [[planet]] [[Takodana]], when the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] led a group of three fugitives from the First Order into the structure. Kanata, an old friend of Solo's, recognized the smuggler shortly after he entered and cried out to him, causing everyone in the castle to turn their attention to the new-comers<ref name="TFA" /> including GA-97<ref name="TFAn">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' novelization]]</ref> and those seated at the [[fighting droid]] table he was sat against.<ref name="TFA" /> After the crowd lost interest, GA-97 turned his attention to the [[Dengue sisters]], a group of three [[Culisetto]]s [[gambling]] on a table nearby.<ref name="TFAn" />

The sisters' game was interrupted when the dismembered [[Limb|arm]] of the [[junk dealer]] [[Unkar Plutt]] landed on their table, having been tossed by the [[Wookiee]] [[Chewbacca]] after he tore it off defending the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], one of Solo's companions. The sisters tossed the arm away absently and continued with the gambling, but GA-97's attention was drawn to Rey and then her companion, the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]]. Recognizing the astromech as a missing Resistance droid, an internal sequence was activated inside GA-97 which triggered him to send out a compressed signal that was bounced around, coded, decoded, encrypted, and then sent into deep space. The signal was then picked up by the [[protocol droid]] [[C-3PO]] in the [[Resistance base]] on the [[planet]] [[D'Qar]]. Overjoyed, C-3PO relayed the message that BB-8 was on Takodana to [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], who then left for Takodana to collect the droid.<ref name="TFAn" />

[[File:GA-97-SWZ.png|thumb|right|250px|GA-97 served drinks as Maz's castle.]]
Before the Resistance could arrive, the occupants of Kanata's castle were drawn outside by the sound of the First Order's [[Starkiller Base]] firing at the [[Hosnian system]]. In the castle's courtyard they stood and watched as it [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroyed]] the whole [[star system]], and the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]] of the [[New Republic]] with it. Almost immediately after the horrific spectacle was over, the First Order [[Battle of Takodana|attacked]] the castle and quickly destroyed it. Those that survived the destruction were then spared, when the Resistance arrived and fought off the First Order's troops, driving them offworld.<ref name="TFAn" />

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|If you're a friend of Maz, you're a friend of mine. What's the job?|GA-97|<ref name="Outer Rim">{{SWOR|set=Unfinished Business}}</ref>}}
GA-97 was an unassuming droid with masculine programming. He had a bipedal body, with a power plant in its chest and collapsible [[Limb|legs]] to allow for compact storage. It had [[Color|black]] [[sensor]]s and red, yellow and green plating.<ref name="TFAVD" /> When reporting to the Resistance, GA-97 spoke in an [[alien]] [[Language|dialect]].<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:GA-97_puppet.png|thumb|left|200px|GA-97 was a puppet controlled by three puppeteers.]]
GA-97<ref name="TFAVD" /> first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']],<ref name="TFA" /> which was released on [[December 18]], [[2015]].<ref name="Release Date">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-episode-vii-to-open-december-18-2015|text=Star Wars: Episode VII to Open December 18, 2015}}</ref> Its lines were provided by voice actor [[David Acord]], who also provided the voices of several other minor characters in the film including [[Sidon Ithano]], [[Teedo (Niima Outpost)|Teedo]] and [[FN-2199]].<ref name="VA">{{SW|url=news/from-blast-that-x-wing-to-traitor-the-voices-of-star-wars-the-force-awakens|text=From "Blast That X-wing!" to "Traitor!": The Voices of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''}}</ref> The droid was not identified in the film,<ref name="TFA" /> but received a name in ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'', a reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> and released the same day as the film.<ref name="New Books">{{SW|url=news/a-galaxy-of-star-wars-the-force-awakens-books-coming-december-18-first-look|text=A Galaxy of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Books Coming December 18 - UPDATED!}}</ref> The GA-97 model was a puppet capable of walking around when controlled by a team of three puppeteers with a fourth controlling electronic functions.<ref name="Bonus">{{HomeVideoCite|film=7|featurette=Secrets of The Force Awakens: A Cinematic Journey|ftext=Secrets of ''The Force Awakens'': A Cinematic Journey}}</ref>

